  "full_text": "So Peter Gadwa said if he had a lot of siblings, he probably wouldn't feel obligated to have children. I come from a family of eight kids, and they all had kids and stuff. And I even encouraged Brenda to have kids. And you're kind of only allowed so many kids from a set of parents. So there's really, it's not clear that I have, you almost need to damn yourself. This might happen. If you're a good person, maybe you get no afterlife, but if you don't have kids, maybe you get no afterlife, but at least your life's good. Maybe that's like a priest, you know? Maybe a priest doesn't have an afterlife, but at least his life's good, right? Then he just disappears or something, right? Because he doesn't have kids, right? Or maybe they do, I don't know. But anyway, then the question is, well, maybe hell is for those who don't have kids. I don't know. But anyway, so... Maybe everybody who has a kid goes to hell, and the only ones that don't are the ones that live in the spiritual realm, which is non-material. I don't know. So you can't win it. Just stop thinking about it, I guess. But, yeah, I take comfort in it. If I don't have resources, I don't have responsibility. If I do have resources, I do have responsibility. So it's pretty, no point stressing over it.",
